Bindel Refactoring & Monetization Implementation Plan
Bindel is currently a monolithic single-file React 19 application. To scale, improve maintainability, and introduce premium supporter monetization features, we are refactoring it into a highly modular, professional architecture.

🏗️ Target Architecture
We will split src/App.tsx into the following modular structure:

src/
├── App.tsx                    # Lightweight orchestrator
├── main.tsx                   # App mounting point
├── index.css                  # Tailwind CSS import & base styles
├── components/
│   ├── ErrorBoundary.tsx      # Robust error capture component
│   ├── layout/
│   │   ├── Header.tsx         # Responsive header
│   │   ├── Footer.tsx         # App footer status bar
│   │   └── Sidebar.tsx        # SlideMenu (renamed to Sidebar)
│   ├── modals/
│   │   ├── IngestModal.tsx    # Fetch URL modal
│   │   ├── AboutModal.tsx     # Information modal
│   │   ├── SettingsModal.tsx  # API key config modal
│   │   ├── HelpModal.tsx      # How-to modal
│   │   └── SupportModal.tsx   # Buy Me a Coffee widget & benefits
│   ├── editor/
│   │   ├── MarkdownEditor.tsx # Textarea editor for manual tweaks
│   │   ├── MarkdownPreview.tsx# ReactMarkdown renderer with GFM
│   │   ├── FloatingToolbar.tsx# Text selection popup action bar
│   │   └── Lightbox.tsx       # Fullscreen image viewer
│   └── ui/
│       ├── Toast.tsx          # Micro-toast notifications
│       ├── MenuButton.tsx     # Sidebar button component
│       ├── HeaderButton.tsx   # Header action button component
│       ├── ToolbarBtn.tsx     # Floating toolbar button component
│       └── StructureDropdown.tsx # Dropdown for Article/Topic/Book mode
├── hooks/
│   ├── useLocalStorage.ts     # Save & load values from localStorage
│   ├── useTheme.ts            # Light/Dark mode state & system theme Sync
│   ├── useToast.ts            # Manage notifications queue
│   ├── useSelection.ts        # Track client selection positions
│   ├── useGeminiAI.ts         # Encapsulate full & partial polishing requests
│   └── useSupporter.ts        # Manage supporter status logic (Buy Me a Coffee)
├── services/
│   ├── extractor.ts           # Readability fetching via local API / CORS proxy
│   ├── turndown.ts            # HTML to Markdown Turndown compiler configuration
│   ├── gemini.ts              # Gemini API client instantiation
│   └── export.ts              # File download & clipboard helper functions
├── utils/
│   ├── cn.ts                  # Tailwind Merge & Clsx class combiner
│   ├── markdown.ts            # Footnote generation & CSV table parsing
│   └── urls.ts                # URL patterns and content detectors
├── types/
│   └── index.ts               # Shared interfaces (Highlights, Toasts, etc.)
└── constants/
    └── index.ts               # Hardcoded prompts, magic strings, and configuration
🛠️ Step-by-Step Execution Plan
1. Infrastructure & Config Updates
tsconfig.json: Add strict compiler options to enforce strict types:
json
"strict": true,
"noUncheckedIndexedAccess": true,
"noImplicitReturns": true,
"forceConsistentCasingInFileNames": true
.env.example: Add configuration variables for Gemini API and Buy Me a Coffee.
bash
GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here
BUYMEACOFFEE_USERNAME=your_username
BUYMEACOFFEE_WIDGET_ID=optional
2. Core Utilities & Types
Create src/types/index.ts to hold core structures (ToastMessage, Highlight, ViewMode, FontSize, etc.).
Create src/utils/cn.ts to export standard class list merges.
Create src/utils/urls.ts with smart content type detection (html, markdown, url-list, plain) and URL extractors.
Create src/utils/markdown.ts containing the footnote injection and CSV table conversions.
3. Services
Create src/services/turndown.ts for consistent HTML -> Markdown parsing.
Create src/services/gemini.ts for GoogleGenAI SDK wrapper.
Create src/services/export.ts for local exports & copies.
Create src/services/extractor.ts to support fetching URLs using both local server-side parsing (/api/extract) and backup remote CORS proxy methods (corsproxy.io).
4. Hooks
useLocalStorage: State wrapper for persistence.
useTheme: Handles system themes, custom preferences, and updates documentElement.
useToast: Queue manager for notifications.
useSelection: Handles text range selectors and anchor nodes inside the editor canvas.
useGeminiAI: Dispatches model completions using structured templates.
useSupporter: Manages Buy Me a Coffee credentials, unlock statuses, and saves preference states.
5. UI & Layout Components
Split up smaller UI wrappers: Toast, HeaderButton, MenuButton, ToolbarBtn, and StructureDropdown.
Rebuild modulatory components:
ErrorBoundary: Catch render crashes.
Modals: IngestModal, AboutModal, SettingsModal, HelpModal, and SupportModal (highly styling-focused, interactive supporter checkout mockup).
Editor elements: MarkdownEditor, MarkdownPreview, FloatingToolbar, and Lightbox.
Layout: Header, Footer, Sidebar (Sidebar matches old SlideMenu with active animations).
LandingPage: Modularized welcome layout.
6. Integration & Validation
Update App.tsx to act as the central manager, hooking all systems together.
Test compilation using npm run lint and run a local dev server with npm run dev.
Use the browser subagent to visually verify that all buttons, modals, AI integrations, and structural modifications function correctly.
